commit 87952c120e561fb9d6ab59ec20be63ca02dda25f
Author: Dawid Zyla <didny1@gmail.com>
Date:   Tue Oct 27 22:04:01 2026 -0600

    Plan 29 Task 8b: a base letter's spot is clear only where its own strand is nearest (22MZ, ruling P29-14)
    
    na_labels._place_letters took a single-stranded nucleotide's first spot clear of text and lines, whichever strand
    it was nearest: 22MZ's pseudoknot routes runs 2 and 6 side by side, and 7 of its 26 unpaired letters sat nearer
    another strand's line than their own (U57 on run 2's far side). A spot beside or along the strand now counts as
    clear only when no other strand's drawn line is nearer it than its own's (_own_nearest; a tie is its own). The later
    passes (by the drawn outlines, then the rings) are unchanged. No new constant (one inventory row: an array shape).
    
    Test: 22MZ (the whole entry, 63 kB gzipped): 7 -> 3 letters nearer another strand; the 3 left have no spot beside or
    along the strand that is both clear and nearest their own, and are placed by the outline pass.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

